<!DOCTYPE html>
<!--
  UCPS 6-gene TNBC risk calculator (Mime RSF + CoxBoost, TCGA-TNBC n = 187)
  CG&T Lab, Department of Biotechnology, IIT Hyderabad

  Single self-contained page: HTML + CSS + JavaScript only, no PHP code and no
  external files (both logos are embedded). The calculation runs in the
  visitor's browser; uploaded files are not sent to the server.
  Same model, formula and cutoff as app.R:
    Risk score = sum_i BETA_i * (x_i - TRAIN_MEAN_i),  x = log2(TPM + 1)

  Colours: header and footer use darker shades of the IITH logo blue (#2E3191;
  CMYK C100 M100 Y0 K0 in the IITH logo booklet).
-->
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>TNBC Risk Calculator | CG&amp;T Lab, IIT Hyderabad</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --iith-blue: #23267A; --iith-blue-dark: #171950;
    --high: #d9534f; --low: #5cb85c;
    --ink: #222; --muted: #5f6368; --line: #dde1e6; --soft: #f5f6fa;
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }
  body { margin: 0; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: var(--ink); background: #fff; line-height: 1.55; }
  a { color: var(--iith-blue); }
  .container { max-width: 1120px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 16px; }

  /* ---------- header ---------- */
  header.site { position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 10; background: var(--iith-blue); color: #fff; }
  header.site .container { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 16px; padding-top: 10px; padding-bottom: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .brand { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; color: #fff; text-decoration: none; }
  .brand img { height: 52px; width: auto; }
  .brand .t1 { font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: bold; line-height: 1.2; }
  .brand .t2 { font-size: .82rem; opacity: .85; }
  nav a { color: #fff; text-decoration: none; margin-left: 18px; font-size: .95rem; opacity: .9; }
  nav a:first-child { margin-left: 0; }
  nav a:hover { opacity: 1; text-decoration: underline; }

  /* ---------- main ---------- */
  .intro { background: var(--soft); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .intro .container { padding-top: 22px; padding-bottom: 20px; }
  h1 { font-size: 1.55rem; margin: 0 0 6px; color: var(--iith-blue); }
  .intro p { margin: 0; color: var(--muted); }
  section { padding: 26px 0 8px; scroll-margin-top: 90px; }
  section h2.sec { font-size: 1.3rem; color: var(--iith-blue); border-bottom: 2px solid var(--line); padding-bottom: 6px; margin: 0 0 14px; }
  h3 { font-size: 1.02rem; margin: 18px 0 6px; }
  .grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 300px 1fr; gap: 22px; align-items: start; }
  @media (max-width: 820px) { .grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } nav a { margin-left: 12px; } }
  .panel { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 6px; padding: 16px; background: var(--soft); }
  .panel h3:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .help { font-size: .9rem; color: var(--muted); }
  button { display: block; width: 100%; margin: 8px 0; padding: 9px 10px; border: 1px solid var(--iith-blue);
           border-radius: 4px; background: #fff; color: var(--iith-blue); font-size: .95rem; cursor: pointer; }
  button.primary { background: var(--iith-blue); color: #fff; }
  button:disabled { opacity: .45; cursor: default; }
  input[type=file] { width: 100%; margin: 6px 0 4px; }
  .msg { padding: 10px 12px; border-radius: 4px; margin: 0 0 12px; font-size: .92rem; display: none; }
  .msg.error { display: block; background: #fdecea; border: 1px solid #f5c2c0; color: #8a1f1b; }
  .msg.warn  { display: block; background: #fff6e0; border: 1px solid #f3dca0; color: #7a5a00; }
  .msg.ok    { display: block; background: #e9f6ec; border: 1px solid #b9e0c3; color: #1e5e2e; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: .9rem; }
  th, td { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 6px 8px; text-align: left; }
  th { background: var(--soft); }
  .tablebox { max-height: 360px; overflow: auto; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 4px; }
  .doc table { margin: 6px 0 12px; }
  .pill { padding: 1px 8px; border-radius: 10px; color: #fff; font-size: .82rem; white-space: nowrap; }
  .pill.High-Risk { background: var(--high); } .pill.Low-Risk { background: var(--low); }
  canvas { width: 100%; height: auto; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 4px; background: #fff; }
  .summary { margin: 0 0 10px; font-size: .95rem; font-weight: bold; }
  .placeholder { border: 1px dashed var(--line); border-radius: 6px; padding: 28px 16px; text-align: center; }
  .doc p, .doc li { font-size: .95rem; }
  .doc ul, .doc ol { padding-left: 22px; margin: 6px 0 10px; }
  .cols { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 28px; }
  @media (max-width: 820px) { .cols { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  code { background: var(--soft); padding: 1px 4px; border-radius: 3px; font-size: .88rem; }
  .cite { background: var(--soft); border-left: 4px solid var(--iith-blue); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 0 4px 4px 0; }
  .todo { background: #fff3a0; color: #222; padding: 0 3px; }
  .hidden { display: none; }
  .grid > *, .cols > * { min-width: 0; }
  .scroll-x { overflow-x: auto; }

  /* ---------- footer ---------- */
  footer.site { background: var(--iith-blue-dark); color: #e6e7f2; margin-top: 36px; font-size: .9rem; }
  footer.site .container { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 1fr 1.3fr; gap: 28px; padding-top: 26px; padding-bottom: 20px; }
  @media (max-width: 820px) { footer.site .container { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  footer.site h4 { color: #fff; font-size: .95rem; margin: 0 0 10px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .04em; }
  footer.site a { color: #fff; }
  footer.site p { margin: 0 0 8px; }
  .logos { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 22px; }
  .logos img.iith { height: 104px; width: auto; }   /* clear space >= 1/8 of logo height kept by the gap/padding */
  .logos img.lab  { height: 88px; width: auto; }
  .member { margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .member b { color: #fff; display: block; }
  .member span { color: #b9bce0; font-size: .85rem; }
  .bottom { border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.15); }
  footer.site .bottom .container { display: block; padding-top: 12px; padding-bottom: 14px; font-size: .82rem; color: #b9bce0; }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<header class="site">
  <div class="container">
    <a class="brand" href="#calculator">
      <img src="data:image/png;base64," alt="CG&amp;T Lab logo">
      <div>
        <div class="t1">TNBC Risk Calculator</div>
        <div class="t2">CG&amp;T Lab &middot; IIT Hyderabad</div>
      </div>
    </a>
    <nav>
      <a href="#calculator">Calculator</a>
      <a href="#about">About</a>
      <a href="#help">Help</a>
    </nav>
  </div>
</header>

<div class="intro">
  <div class="container">
    <h1>6-Gene Signature Prognostic Risk Calculator (TNBC)</h1>
    <p>Calculates the UCPS risk score and risk group for triple-negative breast cancer (TNBC) patients from the expression of six genes. Your file is processed in your browser and is not uploaded to the server.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<main class="container">

  <!-- ============================ CALCULATOR ============================ -->
  <section id="calculator">
    <h2 class="sec">Calculator</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="panel">
        <h3>Inputs</h3>
        <p class="help">Upload a CSV file with a <b>Patient_ID</b> column and the 6 signature genes, or try the example data first.</p>
        <input type="file" id="file" accept=".csv,text/csv">
        <button class="primary" id="calc" disabled>Calculate Risk Scores</button>
        <button id="loadExample">Load example data</button>
        <hr>
        <h3>Download</h3>
        <button id="dlTable" disabled>Download Table (.csv)</button>
        <button id="dlPlot" disabled>Download Plot (.png)</button>
        <button id="dlTemplate">Download input template (.csv)</button>
        <button id="dlExample">Download example file (.csv)</button>
      </div>

      <div id="results">
        <div id="msg" class="msg"></div>
        <div id="out" class="hidden">
          <p class="summary" id="summary"></p>
          <h3>Risk Score Classification Results</h3>
          <div class="tablebox"><table id="tbl"></table></div>
          <h3>Risk Score Distribution Plot</h3>
          <canvas id="plot" width="1600" height="800"></canvas>
        </div>
        <p class="help placeholder" id="placeholder">Upload a CSV file and click "Calculate Risk Scores", or click "Load example data" to see how the calculator works. Results appear here.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================== ABOUT =============================== -->
  <section id="about" class="doc">
    <h2 class="sec">About</h2>
    <div class="cols">
      <div>
        <h3>What this tool does</h3>
        <p>This calculator applies the UCPS (UPS-stratified cell-derived prognostic signature), a six-gene prognostic model for triple-negative breast cancer. For each patient it returns a risk score and assigns the patient to a High-Risk or Low-Risk group.</p>
        <p>The six genes are HELLS, PUF60, ASPHD1, KRT16, EXOSC4 and RARRES1. They were identified from malignant cells in TNBC single-cell RNA-seq data, and the model was trained on bulk RNA-seq and overall survival of 187 TCGA-TNBC patients.</p>
        <h3>Who it is for</h3>
        <p>Researchers who have bulk RNA-seq data from TNBC samples and want to apply the signature to their own patients.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>What you need</h3>
        <p>A CSV file with one row per patient, a <code>Patient_ID</code> column and one column for each of the six genes, with expression as log2(TPM + 1). Details are in <a href="#help">Help</a>.</p>
        <h3>What you get</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>A table with each patient's risk score and risk group, downloadable as CSV.</li>
          <li>A plot of all patients ordered by score, downloadable as PNG.</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>The model</h3>
        <p>Risk score = &minus;0.4823 &times; HELLS + 0.1275 &times; PUF60 + 0.2826 &times; ASPHD1 + 0.0958 &times; KRT16 + 0.3085 &times; EXOSC4 &minus; 0.2744 &times; RARRES1 &minus; 0.7571</p>
        <p>Each gene stands for its log2(TPM + 1) expression. Patients with a score above &minus;0.1081, the median score of the 187 TCGA-TNBC training patients, are classed as High-Risk.</p>
        <h3>Privacy</h3>
        <p>The calculation runs entirely in your web browser. Your file is never sent to or stored on our server.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- =============================== HELP =============================== -->
  <section id="help" class="doc">
    <h2 class="sec">Help</h2>
    <div class="cols">
      <div>
        <h3>How to use</h3>
        <ol>
          <li>Prepare a CSV file in the format below. You can start from the input template (Download input template).</li>
          <li>Click <b>Choose file</b>, select your file, then click <b>Calculate Risk Scores</b>.</li>
          <li>Read the summary, table and plot, and download them if needed.</li>
        </ol>
        <h3>Input file format</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>One row per patient; patients as rows, genes as columns.</li>
          <li>Required columns, spelled exactly as here: <code>Patient_ID</code>, <code>ASPHD1</code>, <code>EXOSC4</code>, <code>HELLS</code>, <code>KRT16</code>, <code>PUF60</code>, <code>RARRES1</code>. Column order does not matter, and other columns are ignored.</li>
          <li>Expression must be log2(TPM + 1) from bulk RNA-seq, processed as for TCGA, to match the training data. If you have TPM values, convert them first, for example in R with <code>log2(tpm + 1)</code>.</li>
          <li>Every patient needs a numeric value for all six genes; empty or <code>NA</code> values give an error.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Example of the first rows of a valid file:</p>
        <div class="scroll-x">
        <table>
          <tr><th>Patient_ID</th><th>ASPHD1</th><th>EXOSC4</th><th>HELLS</th><th>KRT16</th><th>PUF60</th><th>RARRES1</th></tr>
          <tr><td>Example_01</td><td>4.035</td><td>6.642</td><td>1.479</td><td>6.589</td><td>7.801</td><td>7.984</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Example_02</td><td>1.233</td><td>5.200</td><td>3.313</td><td>3.787</td><td>7.156</td><td>3.582</td></tr>
        </table>
        </div>

      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Example data and expected result</h3>
        <p>The example contains 10 made-up patients (not real patient data), with values in the range seen in TCGA. Click <b>Load example data</b> to run it, or <b>Download example file</b> to test the file upload yourself. You should get <b>10 patients: 4 High-Risk, 6 Low-Risk</b>, with these scores:</p>
        <table>
          <tr><th>Patient_ID</th><th>Risk_Score</th><th>Risk_Group</th></tr>
          <tr><td>Example_01</td><td>1.1531</td><td>High-Risk</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Example_02</td><td>-0.1106</td><td>Low-Risk</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Example_03</td><td>-0.5906</td><td>Low-Risk</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Example_04</td><td>-1.0732</td><td>Low-Risk</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Example_05</td><td>-0.3532</td><td>Low-Risk</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Example_06</td><td>1.1378</td><td>High-Risk</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Example_07</td><td>-0.6133</td><td>Low-Risk</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Example_08</td><td>0.0240</td><td>High-Risk</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Example_09</td><td>-0.0636</td><td>High-Risk</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Example_10</td><td>-0.1173</td><td>Low-Risk</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


</main>

